<BaseLayout title='About | damienrobson'>
  <h1>A bit about me</h1>
  <p>Hi, I'm Damien, but you can call me Damo.</p>

  <p>
    By day, I work as an accessibility specialist, helping teams build software
    and websites that work seamlessly for everyone—regardless of ability,
    device, or context.
  </p>

  <p>
    By night (or weekend, depending on how much coffee I've had), I write about
    what I learn along the way.
  </p>

  <h2>Why I care about accessibility</h2>

  <p>
    For me, digital accessibility isn't just about guidelines and WCAG
    criteria—it's about empathy and equity. Behind every broken screen reader
    experience or unnavigable form is a real person trying to get something
    done.
  </p>

  <p>
    I believe learning accessibility should feel approachable, not overwhelming.
    You don't need to know every technical spec overnight to start making a
    positive impact.
  </p>

  <h2>What you'll find here</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Practical Tips</strong>: Simple techniques to make your code and
      designs more inclusive.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Reflections</strong>: Thoughts on current web trends, digital
      rights, and user experience.
    </li>

    <li>
      <strong>Resources</strong>: Guides and tools that I personally rely on in
      my daily work.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Beyond the screen</h2>

  <p>
    When I'm not auditing websites or obsessing over colour contrast ratios, you
    can usually find me spending time with the wife and kids, gaming or
    procrastinating.
  </p>

  <p>
    Want to chat about accessibility, collaborate, or just say hello? Feel free
    to reach out via <a
      href='https://www.linkedin.com/in/damien-r-4b9b37371/'
      target='_blank'
      rel='noreferrer'>my LinkedIn profile (opens in a new tab)</a
    >!
  </p>
</BaseLayout>
